# Citation metadata of kshana-bench, the benchmark (specification, manifests, scorer, baselines and
# public results) as a deposit of its own. The engine's own metadata is ../CITATION.cff.
# DOI: to be filled after deposit (the owner deposits on Zenodo; no DOI exists yet).
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "kshana-bench: open tasks, splits and metrics for GNSS interference detection, timing holdover, spacecraft telemetry anomalies and smartphone positioning"
message: "If you use kshana-bench, please cite it using this metadata, and cite each result by its citation id (kb-...)."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Ashforde OÜ"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana"
url: "https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana/blob/main/docs/BENCH.md"
abstract: >-
  An open benchmark: task definitions, split rules, truth rules and metrics (bench/SPEC.md,
  spec 2.2.0), dataset manifests with licence and redistribution status, the scorer and
  baselines in the Kshana engine, and the public results with stable citation ids. Datasets
  that may not be redistributed (JammerTest, TEXBAT, GSDC) are referenced and fetched, never
  included. Every score is MODELLED and describes a log or a corpus, never a product.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - GNSS
  - interference
  - timing holdover
  - anomaly detection
  - smartphone positioning
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: "2.2.0"
